ACE gperf
=========

ACE gperf is ACE's adaptation of GNU gperf, the perfect hash function
generator. It generates C++17 code for recognizing a set of keywords with a
single lookup.

The detailed manual is in `ace_gperf.texi`. The `GNUmakefile` builds the
`ace_gperf` executable and runs the configured code-generation regression
tests.

ACE gperf is also used by TAO's IDL compiler to generate operation-dispatch
tables.
